invariant: INV-38
file: tls_write.c
catches: tcp_blocking_key_limit
reason: ch_writable_len does not count the KeyUpdate record ch_write sends
  when a write crosses an AES-GCM key's ceiling, so the answer's records
  run 27 bytes past cap there, and the Zig API's all-or-nothing write
  would hand ch_write an output it cannot take. The cap sweep at the
  ceiling and the exact rows under it object.

--- old
    size_t rest = left > CH_KEY_UPDATE_RECORD_LEN ? left - CH_KEY_UPDATE_RECORD_LEN : 0;
--- new
    size_t rest = left;
